description: Arch PKGBUILD conventions for SynapseOS native packages
globs: packages/**/PKGBUILD
alwaysApply: false
---

# PKGBUILD Rules

- Keep recipes source-based (`git+https`, tracked files). Do not vendor binary `.pkg.tar.*`.
- Use `x86_64` or `any`. Rust packages keep `-C target-cpu=x86-64-v3`.
- Bind services to localhost when they are AI gateways (`127.0.0.1`).
- Prefer tracked files under the package dir over gitignored `src/` for gate-checked assets.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — gate-checked greeter lives only in gitignored src/
install -Dm644 src/sddm-theme/Main.qml "$pkgdir/usr/share/sddm/themes/ps2-xfce/Main.qml"

# ✅ GOOD — tracked recipe copy with upstream fallback
sddm_src="$startdir/sddm-theme"
install -Dm644 "${sddm_src}/Main.qml" "$pkgdir/usr/share/sddm/themes/ps2-xfce/Main.qml"
```
